From 325560ec3b78a162d3b010599395c751775f4510 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: haowen1993 <39072333+haowen1993@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:08:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] rebuild(text): re-align the Chinese card-text series onto
 the current card-art series
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The series could not be applied at all: its patches were generated from a branch
built on an EARLIER card-art series, and they patch `preferencesStore.ts` — the file
both series share. Two things had moved underneath them:

  * `restoreArtLanguage` was deleted, so the patches' context no longer anchored.
  * `artLanguage` went from a forced `"zhs"` back to `"auto"`, which is the line
    their hunks were positioned against.

Replaying the old commits does not work either: the earliest of them predates the
`restoreCardTextLanguage` fix, so cherry-picking it reintroduces a version that
resolves an absent persisted value to `"auto"` — the exact defect that fix exists
to prevent. The final state is taken directly instead.

The shared files are resolved in favour of the current art series, and only the
card-text additions are carried: `cardTextLocale.ts` and the `cardTextLanguage`
preference in `preferencesStore`, the card-text strings in the `settings.json`
catalogs (both `cardTextLanguage*` and the `artLanguage*` keys the art series
contributes), and the parity test's `zhs` entry.

Only three commits of the old history are kept — the sidecar generator, the rulings
translation, and its quality floor — because those are the parts that were already
independent of the shared files.
